---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const facts = [
  { role: 'Lecturer in Earth Observation', org: 'UCL Geography', href: 'https://profiles.ucl.ac.uk/94679-martin-mokros' },
  { role: 'ARIA Creator', org: '3DTreePrint project', href: 'https://aria.org.uk/opportunity-spaces/engineering-ecosystem-resilience/opportunity-seeds?cardId=3dtreeprint' },
  { role: 'Fellow', org: 'National Centre for Earth Observation', href: 'https://www.nceo.ac.uk/our-research/missions/biomass/' },
  { role: 'Chair', org: '3DForEcoTech (COST Action)', href: 'https://3dforecotech.eu' },
  { role: 'Award', org: 'UCL Open Science & Scholarship, 2025', href: 'https://www.ucl.ac.uk/social-historical-sciences/news/2025/oct/ucl-geography-lecturer-wins-open-science-award-global-collaboration-forest-research' },
];
---
<Base title="About — Martin Mokroš">
  <div class="wrap page-head">
    <div class="eyebrow">About</div>
    <h1>Martin Mokroš</h1>
  </div>
  <section><div class="wrap"><div class="about-grid">
    <div>
      <div class="portrait">
        <img src="/media/portrait.jpg" alt="Martin Mokroš surveying with a backpack-mounted mobile LiDAR scanner" style="object-fit:cover;transform:scale(1.4);transform-origin:44% 26%;filter:saturate(.7) contrast(.96) brightness(1.04) sepia(.07)" />
      </div>
      <ul class="factlist">
        {facts.map((f) => (
          <li>
            <b>{f.role}</b>
            <a href={f.href} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{f.org}</a>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="big">I build the tools that let us see forests in three dimensions and I care most about the moment someone who isn't a remote-sensing specialist can actually use them.</p>
      <p>I'm a Lecturer in Earth Observation at UCL and a fellow of the National Centre for Earth Observation, and my work spans the whole 3D measurement pipeline: I design and build low-cost laser scanners, benchmark the sensors and software the field relies on, turn raw point clouds into forest structure, carbon and biodiversity, and use machine learning for problems like tree-species classification.</p>
      <p>Right now I lead two projects and field works under <b>3DTreePrint</b> (ARIA) across UK woodlands and <b>Scanning Together</b> (NCEO) in the tropics. Translating and scaling methods from national inventory plots to city streets to community forests in Madagascar. Around the research I supervise postdocs and PhD students, convene three UCL modules and train scientists at international summer schools, with 40+ papers, 3,000+ citations, and a stubborn commitment to open data, shared standards and reproducible tools.</p>
      <div class="about-cta">
        <a class="btn" href="mailto:m.mokros@ucl.ac.uk">Email me →</a>
        <a class="btn ghost" href="https://uk.linkedin.com/in/martinmokros" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Follow me on LinkedIn →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div></div></section>
</Base>
